from their own vanilla download; they contain no Mojang code.

(b) Data derived from Mojang's server

Builds read the user's own vanilla download under ref/ (see section 3) and embed
data derived from it: the registries, block and item data and data pack
(crates/mc-data), the packet ids (crates/mc-protocol) and the language files
(crates/mc-text). None of that data is committed; it is Mojang's, not relicensed
here.

One exception is committed in source form: the witty comments and profile report
comments that Mojang's CrashReport prints (CRASH_NUGGETS and PROFILE_NUGGETS in
crates/mc-game-core/src/crash_report.rs). They are kept so that crash and
profiling reports read like vanilla's. They are Mojang's text, not relicensed
here.

